## remove-evaluation.soar -- selection-world: 1 proposal, 1 compare, 1 application.

## ---- operator proposal ----

## Propose remove-evaluation: the evaluated operator is no longer proposed in the superstate (v2.30).
## Through v2.29 it was proposed when the operator was no longer a tied ^item. An operator also leaves the item set when a
## preference made from its own evaluation filters it out (a failure-cutoff worst preference); removing the evaluation
## then retracted that preference, the operator returned to the tie and was evaluated again, in a loop (seen with
## iterative-step tie-impasse, cost-metric unit and optimize true).
sp {selection-world*propose*selection*remove-evaluation
   :default
   (state <s> ^name selection
             -^item <item>
              ^superstate <ss>
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<evaluation> ^super-operator <item>)
  -(<ss> ^operator <item> +)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <operator> +, =, >)
   (<operator> ^name remove-evaluation
               ^evaluation <evaluation>)}

## ---- evaluate / compare ----

## Preference for selection remove-evaluation.
sp {selection-world*compare*selection*remove-evaluation
   :default
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^operator <op1> +
                        { <> <op1> <op2> }  +)
   (<op1> ^name remove-evaluation)
   (<op2> ^name << decrement-remaining-operators init-current-evaluation-depth >>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op1> > <op2>)
}

## ---- operator application ----

## Apply remove-evaluation -> sets evaluation.
sp {selection-world*apply*remove-evaluation
   :default
   (state <s> ^operator <op>
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<op> ^name remove-evaluation
               ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<evaluation> ^super-operator <item>)
-->
   (write (crlf) |Remove | <evaluation> | as there is no longer the tied item: | <item>)
   (<s> ^evaluation <evaluation> -)
}
